@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Required inference provider-contract follow-up
+
+Owner: Phosphor fork maintainers. Status: open.
+
+The upstream refresh retains already selected patch 0058. Its eight provider-ID
+references enforce the existing required external Claude/Codex policy, invalidate
+cached model facts on route changes, and translate authenticated catalogue facts.
+They do not add a new provider policy. The new upstream literal ratchet accounts
+for this pre-existing downstream behavior explicitly.
+
+Remove these references and their baseline entries when the provider SDK exposes
+required external model catalogue admission and route-scoped cache invalidation.
+Move the adapter into Account Pooler, preserve child credential isolation and
+fail-closed start/resume behavior, and prove the existing required inference
+suites before retiring the core implementation. Do not remove the guard by
+allowing local credential fallback.
